cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the study code, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "cpmaudit: auditing the instability of individual predictions from clinical risk models"
abstract: >-
  A Python package that bootstraps the complete model-building process of a
  binary-outcome clinical risk model to quantify individual-level prediction and
  decision instability, calibration and clinical-utility instability,
  optimism-corrected performance, predictive multiplicity, sample-size adequacy
  and the transport of instability to external populations, with pre-agreed
  stability policies for model governance. The repository also contains a fully
  reproducible study of ICU mortality models developed in MIMIC-IV and evaluated
  in 205 eICU-CRD hospitals, with SHA-256 provenance records for every output.
type: software
authors:
